 "wingChainReason": "Folded bat wings (Meshy modelled them like a cloak: wrist at the top, fingers to the ground). Finger fan per wing with hand-picked tips from a rest ownership check (tailward bulge, low outer tip, forward-lower corner; GLB verts L 3295/6465/6296, R 2584/5427/5036), anchorR 0.10; Move flap from DEF-read keys with the downstroke deepened to a -80/-88/-80 plateau (flap unfitted), no fold/droop on the downstroke, fan held -0.3 at the level crossings, twist +15 at the downstroke peak (wing_chain twist, 964c8256a6), open capped at 0.85; left-wing region excludes a 43-vert strand by the left foot that the arm bone was lifting. Upstroke now reads as a ribbed membrane; downstroke hangs beside/below the belly (still curled vs the DEF). Scratch series wx1-wx7, worker_d/WING_FAN_RECIPE_halcyon_x1-x5.md; user accepted X6 2026-09-28.",
